<% content_for :title, "Refund & Cancellation Policy" %>

<main class="policy">
  <div class="policy__wrap">
    <header class="policy__head">
      <p class="policy__kicker">Salato</p>
      <h1 class="policy__title">Refund &amp; Cancellation Policy</h1>
      <p class="policy__meta">Last updated <%= Date.current.strftime("%-d %B %Y") %></p>
    </header>

    <section class="policy__intro">
      <p>
        This policy explains when and how you can get a refund for tickets bought on
        Salato, and what happens if an event is cancelled, postponed, or changed.
        Salato is the platform that organisers use to sell tickets; the event itself
        belongs to the organiser. That means the organiser sets the refund terms for
        their event, within the limits set out here, and those terms are shown to you
        before you pay.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="policy__section" id="how-payments-work">
      <h2>How payments and refunds flow</h2>
      <p>
        When you buy a ticket, your payment is processed by our payment partner and
        settles to the organiser's own account, minus Salato's platform commission.
        Salato does not hold your money and does not operate a wallet or balance.
        Approved refunds are returned through the same payment partner to the original
        payment method you used — the same M-Pesa number or card. We cannot refund to
        a different account, in cash, or by any other route.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="policy__section" id="organiser-refunds">
      <h2>Refunds set by the organiser</h2>
      <p>
        Each event carries the refund terms its organiser has chosen. Before you check
        out, you'll see whether that event's tickets are refundable and up to what
        point. Common options an organiser may set include:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Non-refundable</strong> — all sales final once purchased.</li>
        <li><strong>Refundable up to a deadline</strong> — for example, up to 48 hours before the event start time.</li>
        <li><strong>Fully refundable</strong> — cancel any time before the event.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If a request falls within the organiser's stated terms, we'll process the
        refund. If it falls outside them, the organiser decides whether to approve it.
        Whatever an organiser sets, it cannot override the guarantees in the next
        section.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="policy__section" id="cancelled">
      <h2>If an event is cancelled</h2>
      <p>
        If an organiser cancels an event, every ticket holder is entitled to a full
        refund of the ticket price, regardless of the event's normal refund terms.
        Salato notifies all affected ticket holders by email and WhatsApp, and refunds
        are processed to the original payment method. This is the one case where the
        organiser's own terms do not apply — a cancelled event is always refundable.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="policy__section" id="postponed">
      <h2>If an event is postponed or moved</h2>
      <p>
        If an organiser changes the date, time, or venue of an event, your existing
        ticket normally stays valid for the new details, and we'll let you know what
        has changed. If the new date, time, or venue doesn't work for you, you may
        request a full refund of the ticket price. Contact us at
        <a href="mailto:hello@salato.app">hello@salato.app</a> with your order details
        and we'll arrange it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="policy__section" id="material-change">
      <h2>If the event is materially different</h2>
      <p>
        If an event turns out to be materially different from how it was advertised —
        for example, the headline act or main feature that was promised does not appear
        — you may be entitled to a refund even where tickets were sold as
        non-refundable. Raise it with us and we'll review the case with the organiser.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="policy__section" id="fees">
      <h2>Fees and partial refunds</h2>
      <p>
        Where a refund is due, we refund the ticket price you paid. Any payment
        processing fees charged by the payment partner may be non-refundable, and this
        will be made clear at checkout where it applies. Salato's platform commission
        is refunded as part of a full refund for a cancelled event.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="policy__section" id="how-to-request">
      <h2>How to request a refund</h2>
      <p>To ask for a refund:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Email <a href="mailto:hello@salato.app">hello@salato.app</a> from the address you used to buy the ticket.</li>
        <li>Include your order number, the event name, and the reason for the request.</li>
        <li>We'll acknowledge your request and, where it needs the organiser's decision, pass it to them.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We aim to acknowledge requests within a few business days. Once a refund is
        approved, the time it takes to reach your account depends on the payment
        partner and your bank or mobile money provider — usually a few business days.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="policy__section" id="no-show">
      <h2>Missed events and used tickets</h2>
      <p>
        Tickets are not refundable if you simply do not attend, or if you arrive after
        the event has ended. A ticket whose QR code has already been scanned for entry
        counts as used and cannot be refunded.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="policy__section" id="disputes">
      <h2>Disputes between buyers and organisers</h2>
      <p>
        If you and an organiser disagree about a refund, contact us and we'll help
        mediate. Where an event has clearly not been delivered as advertised, Salato
        may step in, and can suspend an organiser from selling further tickets. If you
        raise a chargeback with your bank, the payment partner's dispute process
        applies, and we will provide the order, delivery, and entry records as evidence.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="policy__section" id="organisers">
      <h2>For organisers</h2>
      <p>
        As an organiser, you're responsible for setting fair refund terms, honouring
        them, and refunding in full when you cancel an event. Because refunds come out
        of funds settled to your account, keep enough balance available to cover
        refunds you may owe. Repeatedly failing to honour refunds or cancellations may
        lead to suspension under our Acceptable Use Policy.
      </p>
    </section>

    <footer class="policy__foot">
      <p>
        Questions about a refund or this policy? Email
        <a href="mailto:hello@salato.app">hello@salato.app</a>.
      </p>
    </footer>
  </div>
</main>

<style>
  .policy {
    --ink: #150D3A;
    --violet: #7620B1;
    --orange: #FC8027;
    --mist: #F7F4FB;
    background: var(--mist);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: "Inter Tight", "Trebuchet MS", system-ui, sans-serif;
    padding: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 5rem) 1.25rem clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6rem);
  }
  .policy__wrap { max-width: 46rem; margin: 0 auto; }
  .policy__head { padding-bottom: 2rem; border-bottom: 2px solid rgba(21,13,58,.1); margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .policy__kicker {
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono", ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: .8rem; letter-spacing: .04em; color: var(--violet);
    margin: 0 0 .75rem;
  }
  .policy__title {
    font-family: "Outfit", "Trebuchet MS", sans-serif;
    font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.05;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 3.2rem);
    margin: 0 0 .9rem;
    background: linear-gradient(100deg, var(--violet), var(--orange));
    -webkit-background-clip: text; background-clip: text; color: transparent;
  }
  .policy__meta { margin: 0; color: rgba(21,13,58,.6); font-size: .95rem; }
  .policy__intro p, .policy__section p, .policy__foot p { line-height: 1.65; }
  .policy__intro p { font-size: 1.08rem; margin: 0 0 2.5rem; }
  .policy__section { margin-bottom: 2.75rem; }
  .policy__section h2 {
    font-family: "Outfit", "Trebuchet MS", sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.4rem; font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 .8rem;
    padding-left: .85rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--orange);
  }
  .policy__section p { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .policy__section ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.25rem; }
  .policy__section li { line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: .55rem; }
  .policy__section strong { font-weight: 600; }
  .policy a { color: var(--violet); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  .policy a:hover { color: var(--orange); }
  .policy__foot {
    margin-top: 3rem; padding-top: 1.75rem;
    border-top: 2px solid rgba(21,13,58,.1);
    color: rgba(21,13,58,.7); font-size: .95rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .policy__section h2 { font-size: 1.2rem; }
  }
</style>
